      "output_text": "The fog in Oakhaven did not roll in; it descended, heavy and wet, settling into the marrow of the town like a damp chill that no amount of coal could dispel. It was November, and the river, a sluggish serpent of gray water, churned against the pilings of the wharves with a sound like grinding teeth. For Elias Thorne, the fog was not merely weather; it was a curtain, and he was the only one who knew what lay behind it.\n\nElias sat in the back room of *The Gilded Anchor*, a tavern that smelled perpetually of stale beer and brine.",
